# ALTIER · Page 1 — environment
#
# Copy to page1/.env and fill in. NEVER commit the real file: page1/.gitignore excludes it.
# Nothing in this codebase hardcodes a key, and no API response ever returns one — /health
# reports only whether a key is PRESENT, never its value.

# --- Gemini (the written "today's fit" explanation) ---
# gemini-2.5-flash, the GENERATE model. Note that gemini-embedding is a text-embedding model
# and cannot write prose. Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — the free tier is
# enough for page 1.
# Without this, /today still works: it falls back to the deterministic reason and says so.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Supabase (auth, profiles, pgvector, storage) ---
# Project settings -> API. The ANON key is safe in a client and is what the backend uses to act
# AS THE USER, so Row-Level Security applies to every query.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The SERVICE key BYPASSES Row-Level Security. Backend only, never in the Expo app, never in
# a client bundle. Used solely by POST /admin/seed-rules to write the shared rules table.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=

# --- CORS ---
# Comma-separated origins the API will accept. Defaults to "*" for Expo development, which is
# fine on a laptop and must be narrowed before this is reachable from the internet.
ALTIER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=*

# --- vecdb (the author's FAISS vector database + RAG service; powers /ask and the product pool) ---
# Path to the vectorDB checkout. Defaults to ~/vectorDB, then ASTRAWEAR/vectorDB. Needs faiss-cpu
# in this venv. Without it, /ask answers 503 and /today uses the seed looks.
VECDB_DIR=

# --- live product search (grows the candidate pool via POST /pool/ingest) ---
# SerpApi Google Shopping: free tier is 250 searches/month, non-commercial. Or an eBay Browse token.
SERPAPI_KEY=
